An inline-block in Ladybird now takes no baseline from a block-level
table inside it, so below such a table it sits on its bottom margin
edge. Chrome 158 and Firefox 151 give the same baseline and box height
in all eight cases of the new test, run with engine-compare. WebKit
26.5 agrees except in the two cases that depend on the font’s ascent.

Blink’s BlockLayoutAlgorithm::PropagateBaselineFromBlockChild() returns
early for a table child when it computes an inline-block’s baseline,
and Gecko’s nsBlockFrame::GetBaselineBOffset() skips a table wrapper
frame when it exports a baseline for line layout. This paragraph comes
from reading their sources, not running them.
